2.0.1","description":"","creator":{"login":"cebe","id":189796,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4OTc5Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/189796?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cebe","html_url":"https://github.com/cebe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cebe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cebe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cebe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cebe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cebe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cebe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cebe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cebe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cebe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":0,"closed_issues":437,"state":"closed","created_at":"2014-07-23T20:59:59Z","updated_at":"2018-03-05T14:59:21Z","due_on":"2014-12-07T08:00:00Z","closed_at":"2014-12-07T16:32:02Z"},"comments":17,"created_at":"2014-11-21T20:08:17Z","updated_at":"2014-11-24T11:42:37Z","closed_at":"2014-11-23T00:55:30Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"I have filtering in controller:\n\n```\n$searchModel = new TaskMimicSearch();\n$query = $searchModel->search(Yii::$app->request->get());\n\n$dataProvider = new ActiveDataProvider([\n    'query' => $query\n]);\n\nreturn $this->render('index', ['dataProvider' => $dataProvider]);\n```\n\n`$searchModel->search` returns instance of `\\yii\\db\\ActiveQuery` without joins, only with `WHERE` condition (called `andFilterWhere` methods). Here is part of var_dump of $query variable;\n\n```\n...\n [\"where\"]=>\n  array(3) {\n    [0]=>\n    string(3) \"and\"\n    [1]=>\n    array(1) {\n      [\"type\"]=>\n      string(8) \"ipoEvent\"\n    }\n    [2]=>\n    array(4) {\n      [0]=>\n      string(7) \"BETWEEN\"\n      [1]=>\n      string(9) \"finish_at\"\n      [2]=>\n      object(yii\\db\\Expression)#148 (2) {\n        [\"expression\"]=>\n        string(26) \"(NOW() - INTERVAL 1 MONTH)\"\n        [\"params\"]=>\n        array(0) {\n        }\n      }\n      [3]=>\n      object(yii\\db\\Expression)#150 (2) {\n        [\"expression\"]=>\n        string(5) \"NOW()\"\n        [\"params\"]=>\n        array(0) {\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n...\n```\n\nAfter executing data provider instance have 0 items. I watched DB Log in Yii Debugger and i see that: http://i.gyazo.com/6ad41426d938307540e3845efff3f05a.png\n`COUNT(*)` goes **AFTER** `SELECT(*)` _only for this filtering query_.\n\nAs you can see on screenshot, the builded sql statement looks like: \n\n```\nSELECT * FROM `tasks` WHERE (`type`='ipoEvent') AND (`finish_at` BETWEEN (NOW() - INTERVAL 1 MONTH) AND NOW()) LIMIT 20\n```\n\nThis query **works fine then i execute it in PhpMyAdmin**, returns 4 items (copy from Yii Debugger, paste to PhpMyAdmin query window).\n\nI don't understand why this query returns 0 items if there is 4 items satisfying the specified condition and why ActiveDataProvider queries items first and _then_ queries COUNT of items (all other queries without INTERVAL calcalations works fine and ActiveDataProvider does COUNT first, SELECT - after).\n","closed_by":{"login":"cebe","id":189796,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4OTc5Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/189796?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cebe","html_url":"https://github.com/cebe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cebe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cebe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cebe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cebe/starr